@startuml PDA_NoOrder_Use_Case
left to right direction
title PDA No-Order Reporting — Use Case Diagram

actor "Line Operator" as Op
actor "Supervisor\n(optional)" as Sup

rectangle "PDA No-Order Reporting" {

  usecase "Login" as UC01
  usecase "Select line / group / machine" as UC02
  usecase "Start job" as UC03
  usecase "Pause / resume" as UC04
  usecase "Report completion" as UC05
  usecase "Query history" as UC06
  usecase "Scan barcode" as UCScan
  usecase "Exception / anomaly check\n(optional ops)" as UC07
}

Op --> UC01
Op --> UC02
Op --> UC03
Op --> UC04
Op --> UC05
Op --> UC06

Sup ..> UC06 : review records
Sup ..> UC07 : ops review (if used)

UC01 ..> UCScan : <<include>>
UC02 ..> UCScan : <<include>>
UC03 ..> UCScan : <<include>>
UC05 ..> UCScan : <<include>>

note right of UCScan
  Honeywell scan SDK / wedge input
  (employee QR, device code, batch / drawing)
end note

note bottom of UC07
  Delivered as ops tooling (anomaly scan / export);
  not required for core start–report happy path.
end note

@enduml

' 1. Primary actor is the line operator; supervisor is optional for history / anomaly review.
' 2. Core flow: Login → select line/group/machine → Start → Report → Query; Pause/resume is supported.
' 3. Scan barcode is included by login, selection, start, and report for shop-floor speed.
